The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
} __packed __aligned(COMMANDLIST_ALIGNMENT);
```
Reason:
The packing annotation (`__packed`) applied to the `CommandList` structure caused the `atomic_t` member to become misaligned. This misalignment resulted in unaligned access errors during boot on the HP rx3600 ia64 machine, as the structure was not intended to be sent to the controller in a packed format.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
} __aligned(COMMANDLIST_ALIGNMENT);
```
Reason:
Removing the `__packed` annotation restores the natural alignment of the `atomic_t` member within the `CommandList` structure, preventing unaligned access errors and allowing the system to boot correctly on the HP rx3600 ia64 machine.

